{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB12141 - MONDO_15165",
  "verbalization": "Gilteritinib is associated with Acute Myeloid Leukemia And Myelodysplastic Syndromes Related To Topoisomerase Type 2 Inhibitor through a series of indirect pathways. The drug is indicated for Acute Myeloblastic Leukemia Without Maturation, which in turn is linked to Azacitidine and Mitoxantrone, both of which are associated with this condition. While Gilteritinib is primarily known for its use in treating acute myeloid leukemia, its indirect connection to topoisomerase type 2 inhibitor-related myeloid disorders emerges through its role in activating or enhancing the activity of these inhibitors in the context of leukemia. The evidence suggests that Gilteritinib may contribute to the pathophysiology of these conditions by influencing the cellular response to topoisomerase type 2 inhibitors, though the exact mechanism remains unclear. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Gilteritinib to be repurposed for treating myeloid malignancies associated with topoisomerase type 2 inhibitors, based on the observed clinical and pharmacological relationships.",
